stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> PROPOSED: S1 provider configuration registered with a current terms record
    PROPOSED --> NOTICE_PERIOD: S2 notice sent to a tenant with no sector profile
    PROPOSED --> CONSENT_PENDING: S3 consent requested from an RBI, SEBI or IRDAI tenant
    NOTICE_PERIOD --> ELIGIBLE: S4 notice period elapses with no objection
    NOTICE_PERIOD --> OBJECTED: S5 tenant objects
    CONSENT_PENDING --> ELIGIBLE: S6 prior written consent recorded by the signatory
    CONSENT_PENDING --> OBJECTED: S7 tenant declines
    OBJECTED --> ELIGIBLE: S11 tenant withdraws its objection in writing
    ELIGIBLE --> SUSPENDED: S8 terms lapse, security hold, or a provider-imposed change
    SUSPENDED --> ELIGIBLE: S9 terms renewed or hold lifted with no change in location or data classes
    SUSPENDED --> PROPOSED: S12 the imposed change is accepted as a new configuration
    ELIGIBLE --> WITHDRAWN: S10 tenant withdraws consent or the provider is removed
    ELIGIBLE --> CONSENT_PENDING: S13 tenant profile becomes regulated without prior written consent on record
    OBJECTED --> [*]
    WITHDRAWN --> [*]

    note right of ELIGIBLE
      Only ELIGIBLE receives traffic.
      Failover stays inside the ELIGIBLE set.
      Every transition is kept append-only
      so the set on any past date is a query.
    end note
